  "data": {
    "accession": "PXD011704",
    "title": "QToF Cross-linking Optimisation",
    "additionalAttributes": [],
    "projectDescription": "Optimising the parameters for cross-link analysis using a QToF mass spectrometer. We performed triplicate analysis of 6 different collision energy ramps to determine the optimal energy for cross-link fragmentation.",
    "sampleProcessingProtocol": "BSA was cross-linked with BS3 d0/d12 at 100 times molar excess of cross-linker. The sample was digested in solution with Trypsin and enriched as per the protocol described in Leitner, Alexander, Thomas Walzthoeni, and Ruedi Aebersold. \"Lysine-specific chemical cross-linking of protein complexes and identification of cross-linking sites using LC-MS/MS and the xQuest/xProphet software pipeline.\" Nature protocols 9.1 (2014): 120 Samples were analysed on a Synapt G2-Si using DDA with various collision energies",
    "dataProcessingProtocol": "Data were analysed using PLGS with slow-slow deisotoping to achieve MGF files. These were processed in MSConvert with 32 bit encoding to mzXML format. These files were processed in xQuest",
